## Source audit and change

- Pinned `MQClientInstance.consumeMessageDirectly` passes the same
  `MessageExt` instance through the selected Push consume service. The Java
  callback and `resetRetryAndNamespace` call virtual topic, queue ID, broker,
  message ID, setter and display methods.
- Added public `MessageExtSubtype` with downcastable custom fields and hooks
  for those selected virtual methods. `MessageExt::clone` shares the runtime
  adapter; serialization/deserialization omit it. Exported the trait from the
  Common crate and `rocketmq-classic` facade.
- Added an invoked Java custom subclass and matching Rust direct-consume case.
  It exercises initial topic assignment, retry-topic restoration, namespace
  removal, queue/broker/message getters and setters, custom fields, and
  `toString`. All 27 direct-consume cases compare successfully.
- Updated the Phase 6, Phase 10 and Phase 18 crosswalks and the release
  checklist. The broader inherited `Message`/`MessageExt` override inventory
  remains open.

